      "writtenOn": "2024-12-19T09:25:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Gil for your reply. In fact, this cl introduces a new open-dice wrapper, which differs from all the existing ones. Given the ongoing changes in both upstream dice and this library (e.g., http://pwrev.dev/253672), and that the new make rules are not covered by presubmit, I\u0027m concerned about long-term maintainability. Not everyone is familiar with the Trusty testing setup.\n\nIdeally, we could avoid adding another wrapper and rely on the existing open-dice targets to simplify maintenance. @inseob@google.com and @jaewan@google.com, since you\u0027ve worked on the Trusty build system migration, could you weigh in on whether this is feasible?\n\nIf there\u0027s no alternative, we can proceed with the current approach.",
      "parentUuid": "1028246b_001045ae",
      "revId": "b2fb4846e9a6a4da5a443f3bfb642ca79382c90b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
